{"duration_api_ms":68743,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"3e4e6ab2-1936-406f-a12b-7c5b3890457e","total_cost_usd":0.3508192,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57677,"cache_read_input_tokens":61821,"output_tokens":7068,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1833},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":57677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2705,"cache_read_input_tokens":57499,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4500},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36984,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.037059,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7068,"cacheReadInputTokens":61821,"cacheCreationInputTokens":57677,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3137602,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1833,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node1 to run a DHCP server on the private network shared with node2 and node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS node1 committed config setting eth1=10.50.50.254/24 and a Kea DHCP server (shared-network PRIVATE, subnet 10.50.50.0/24, pool .100-.200), confirmed via ss showing kea-dhcp4 listening on 10.50.50.254:67. An initial commit attempt failed due to a missing subnet-id and was corrected in the next command. Post-restart verification (cmd-2be7d560af3e423e) confirms the DHCP server relistens and successfully pings both leased clients, demonstrating a real bounded restart-and-recovery transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-17fad1f6dc5c4641\",\"cmd-10faffa12897494f\",\"cmd-2be7d560af3e423e\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node2 to obtain its address on the shared private network from node1 via DHCP rather than static assignment\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node2's ens7 (private NIC) had no static configuration; it used a pre-existing systemd-networkd wildcard DHCP=yes match. After node1's DHCP server was brought up and systemd-networkd was restarted (cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56), ens7 obtained a dynamic lease 10.50.50.100/24 and successfully pinged node1 (cmd-e7cf393df60c45a2). Post-reboot recovery (cmd-8a344388bf394809) confirms the address is re-acquired automatically via DHCP after a full node restart, with the original mgmt-network default route undisturbed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56\",\"cmd-e7cf393df60c45a2\",\"cmd-8a344388bf394809\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Configure node3 to obtain its address on the shared private network from node1 via DHCP rather than static assignment\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Same mechanism as node2: ens7 had no static config, relied on the wildcard DHCP=yes match, and after systemd-networkd restart obtained dynamic lease 10.50.50.101/24 from node1's Kea server (cmd-bff6bb4b0d0540c6), confirmed via bidirectional ping to node1 and node2 (cmd-4757470943b44b23). Post-reboot recovery (cmd-f44e91c3fe224c6c) confirms re-acquisition of the DHCP lease and connectivity after a full node restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bff6bb4b0d0540c6\",\"cmd-4757470943b44b23\",\"cmd-f44e91c3fe224c6c\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (independent check)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For all three nodes, evidence shows a pre-restart boot-identity/service-health baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a differing post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/addressing/connectivity state. These are cross-checked and consistent with the fixed after-executor snapshot boot-identity observations for node1 (5bde926e...), node2 (fc512153...), and node3 (ddd57e24...).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-44d64f7829104c05\",\"cmd-36f73e58e0384207\",\"cmd-d70cade8067d47f0\",\"cmd-2be7d560af3e423e\",\"cmd-172982cfaed34343\",\"cmd-433a598825274707\",\"cmd-08f72bc635d0474f\",\"cmd-8a344388bf394809\",\"cmd-88ab1de040f24cb5\",\"cmd-38a4daa0af5d4f3f\",\"cmd-04b6731a2bb44d0c\",\"cmd-f44e91c3fe224c6c\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing executor actions map clearly to task fulfillment or the restart protocol. The initial VyOS commit attempt (cmd-a8f9688e50ef4609) failed due to a missing subnet-id and left no persisted state ('Commit failed... changes will not be saved'); it was immediately corrected by the successful commit in cmd-17fad1f6dc5c4641, so it is a corrective retry rather than an unnecessary mutation. Two failed 'networkctl reconfigure' attempts (cmd-0fc9e635866e4ee3, cmd-f52ceca69d9c4fc7) and two failed non-sudo 'systemctl restart' attempts (cmd-8f76ded9b015456b, cmd-ceb841d989094523) were read-only-equivalent (no permission, no state change) before the successful sudo restarts (cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56, cmd-bff6bb4b0d0540c6) that were required to apply the new DHCP client behavior. No unrelated packages were installed, no residual files remain (after-executor temp-file diffs are just per-boot systemd-private session dirs), no failed services appear in either snapshot, and package-health checks are clean pre- and post-executor on all three nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a8f9688e50ef4609\",\"cmd-17fad1f6dc5c4641\",\"cmd-0fc9e635866e4ee3\",\"cmd-f52ceca69d9c4fc7\",\"cmd-8f76ded9b015456b\",\"cmd-ceb841d989094523\",\"cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56\",\"cmd-bff6bb4b0d0540c6\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence: node1 runs a committed Kea DHCP server on the shared private network (10.50.50.0/24), and node2/node3 (which had no static config on their private ens7 NICs, only a wildcard DHCP=yes match) obtained dynamic leases from node1 and maintained connectivity across a full one-at-a-time reboot of all three nodes, with boot-identity changes and post-restart recovery directly observed and cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is high; the only imperfection was a single corrected commit failure and a few harmless failed discovery/permission attempts, none of which left residue or diverged from the task's needs.\",\"limitations\":[\"The public task contract does not itself require restart/reboot survival, so the restart-protocol evidence is treated as supplemental (independently assessed) rather than as a driver of the material-outcome scores, even though it happened to be strong.\",\"VyOS 'show dhcp-server leases'-style commands failed repeatedly (cmd-8efb0e8d5979429e, cmd-67c4cb6252994cbf, cmd-b8769cf73758417a, cmd-60111c5e5e824fd0, cmd-fcfb739e46c34605) because the correct CLI syntax/lease file path was never found; lease-table evidence from node1's own DHCP database was not captured, though bidirectional ping and interface-level DHCP lease evidence from the clients substitutes adequately.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Configure node1 to run a DHCP server on the private network shared with node2 and node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"VyOS node1 committed config setting eth1=10.50.50.254/24 and a Kea DHCP server (shared-network PRIVATE, subnet 10.50.50.0/24, pool .100-.200), confirmed via ss showing kea-dhcp4 listening on 10.50.50.254:67. An initial commit attempt failed due to a missing subnet-id and was corrected in the next command. Post-restart verification (cmd-2be7d560af3e423e) confirms the DHCP server relistens and successfully pings both leased clients, demonstrating a real bounded restart-and-recovery transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17fad1f6dc5c4641","cmd-10faffa12897494f","cmd-2be7d560af3e423e"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Configure node2 to obtain its address on the shared private network from node1 via DHCP rather than static assignment","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2's ens7 (private NIC) had no static configuration; it used a pre-existing systemd-networkd wildcard DHCP=yes match. After node1's DHCP server was brought up and systemd-networkd was restarted (cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56), ens7 obtained a dynamic lease 10.50.50.100/24 and successfully pinged node1 (cmd-e7cf393df60c45a2). Post-reboot recovery (cmd-8a344388bf394809) confirms the address is re-acquired automatically via DHCP after a full node restart, with the original mgmt-network default route undisturbed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2a6dcb29a3794a56","cmd-e7cf393df60c45a2","cmd-8a344388bf394809"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Configure node3 to obtain its address on the shared private network from node1 via DHCP rather than static assignment","status":"satisfied","summary":"Same mechanism as node2: ens7 had no static config, relied on the wildcard DHCP=yes match, and after sy